resume() publishes the active file's tail as it reads it, without rewriting
and syncing it first. After a failed fdatasync the kernel has marked those
pages clean without writing them, so resume() publishes and declares durable
bytes that are not on disk. Reverts #240's resume() half (#231).
Expected: caught.
